.TH TDE\-NMCTL\-TRAY 1 "November 2026" "tde-nmctl 0.1.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde\-nmctl\-tray \- network status and connections in the system tray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tde\-nmctl\-tray
.RB [ \-\-popup ]
.RI [ "generic TDE and TQt options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde\-nmctl\-tray
shows the state of
.BR NetworkManager (8)
in the system tray of the Trinity panel, like nm\-applet, nm\-tray and the
plasma\-nm applet. It starts at login.
.PP
The icon shows the primary connection: a cable for wired connections, the
signal strength for Wi\-Fi, bars for mobile broadband, a padlock when a VPN
is connected, and a warning sign when the network has no Internet access.
The tooltip lists the active connections.
.PP
A left click opens a popup with
.IP \(bu 2
switches for networking, Wi\-Fi and mobile broadband;
.IP \(bu 2
the active connections with their addresses, an information button and
.BR Disconnect ;
.IP \(bu 2
the Wi\-Fi networks in range, strongest and saved networks first, with
their security and band and a
.B Connect
button, and
.B Connect to Hidden Network
.IP \(bu 2
the VPN connections and other saved connections that can be started now;
.IP \(bu 2
.BR "Edit Connections" ,
which starts
.BR tde\-nmctl (1).
.PP
Connecting to a Wi\-Fi network without a saved connection asks for its
password and creates a connection; the password is stored in TDE Wallet.
Enterprise (802.1X) networks open the connection editor instead.
.PP
The context menu (right click) has the switches,
.BR "Connection Information" ,
which shows the addresses, DNS servers, speed and traffic of the active
connections, the hidden network dialog, the editor, and options for
notifications and starting at login.
.SH SECRET AGENT
The tray registers as a NetworkManager
.I secret agent
for the user's session. When NetworkManager needs a password that belongs
to the user, it asks the agent, which takes it from TDE Wallet (folder
.B tde\-nmctl
of the network wallet) or asks the user. Connections whose passwords are
stored for all users do not need the tray.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
Established, lost and failed connections and VPN changes are announced with
TDE notifications (events of
.BR tde\-nmctl\-tray ),
which can be changed in the Control Center under
.BR "System Notifications" .
.SH TDE NETWORK MANAGER
If TDE's older applet
.B tdenetworkmanager
also starts at login, the tray asks once whether to turn it off. It stays
installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-popup
Open the popup after starting.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/config/tde\-nmctl\-trayrc
.B [General] Autostart=false
stops the tray from starting at login (also set by
.B Start Automatically at Login
in the menu).
.TP
.I /opt/trinity/share/autostart/tde\-nmctl\-tray\-autostart.desktop
The autostart entry.
